<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tyrifjorden</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tyrifjorden is a large lake in Buskerud, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>. Despite its name it is a freshwater lake, not a fjord. It lies at the heart of the Ringerike district, a petty kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> age, and drains southwards into the Drammen River.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tyrifjorden.jpg" alt="Tyrifjorden" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holsfjorden,_Hole.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
